From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:49:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release HTTP handler tasks before completing cancellation

Own and join the handler and disconnect listener on every exit, including
cancellation of the route itself. Preserve receive errors and shield async
cleanup from surrounding AnyIO cancellation. Count tracked requests once,
including cancellation while a completed response is being handed off.

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Rationale: abandoned handlers can retain prompts and overlap later work;
disconnect/response races can also double-decrement the frontend load count.
Quality: no model arithmetic, sampling, scheduler policy or response data changes.
Tests: 15 CPU lifetime regressions and 12 real-HTTP boundary checks using the
candidate-38 Python runtime; original source fails the lifetime regressions.
Upstream status: proposed to the contribution fork; deployment evidence and
source PR are linked in the HTTP cancellation experiment.
